Z||000000||Punkndrublic||09-22-1999||11:31 PM||||I hope I named this part right. Its the part that is attached to the slave cylinder rod and the rotating "rod" part that sticks out of the tranny. The part cracked and broke off on the area were the bolt is to attach it to the tranny. I told the shop that i took it to, to replace the part and bleed the hydrolics. They gave me the "fiero is different" story about how you have to adjust the clutch/linkage to make sure it doesn't drag even if the petal is all the way in. I told them that the system is self adjusting, and they said its "to a point" Are they BSing me? I thought that the clutch was naturally fully engaged if it doesn't have the hydrolics pushing on it.||||reg||3
Z||000001||Pat||09-23-1999||01:21 AM||||That rotating "ROD" part is the clutch fork.<BR>The entire system is totally self-adjusting.<BR>I Developed a system to replace the entire<BR>clutch fork, clutch, pressure plate, and the<BR>drives seals in about 3-4 hours without the<BR>tranny even coming out of the car. And all<BR>that is required is at least 2 good jack <BR>stands and a floor jack. But, don't feel bad<BR>my clutch release lever has a small crack on<BR>one side of it. And since the release lever<BR>only goes on one-way, just don't torque the<BR>bolt down too tight.<P>bye for now.................................||||reg||1
Z||000002||Racer 1||09-23-1999||01:24 AM||||Pontaic made a Upgraded clutch level. The stock lever were made out of to pieces of steel.The new one is all on piece.I broke mine also I think the part cost 30$-90$ cant remeber it was so long ago when mine went kapute!||||reg||14
